{"kind":"report","text":"Bounded technical disposition only; no Source approval, new grant, activation or provider/deployment authority.\n\nReceiver-selected interpretation is the right boundary. A closed internal legacy/partition-v1 proof selector can request the necessary bounded facts, but the selector is not itself authority to assign change/issue. The actual receiver must choose the admissible identity policy from its exact pinned code and, for unchanged declared lane bytes, its independently verified immutable birth lineage. Old receivers retain old sourceName/application/publication behavior and the original three-frame interpretation. A new origin request, producer alias or cached label cannot upgrade them.\n\nThe smaller separation is: keep the producer's default under/nameUnder meaning unchanged; add only a closed bounded proof-collection view, then let the receiving policy derive the privileged identity from those checked facts. If you instead return a mode-specific derived under from the producer, bind/revalidate it to the requested mode and receiving lineage, and never let it substitute for local eligibility. No arbitrary callback, method selector, caller-supplied root/cohort hint, trace/correlation flag or truthy extension of the old boolean selects authority. Unknown modes reject; old boolean calls keep their exact meaning.\n\nSelecting only by destination6 is insufficient for the whole cohort. New issue/change scopes have the same declared digest as older ones, so their own local accepted genesis/create chain must establish partition1/root10 membership before their source/fact/delivery readers can use partition-v1. Membership6 or inbox1 by themselves are also not a new-room discriminator: membership6 already exists in the old invitation-key cohort. Inventory all relevant consumers, including core foreign fact reads, received handlers, origin production, before-send publication checks and replay. Make selection immutable per checked receiver lineage, not a global mutable callback or an ambient context borrowed from a concurrent request. Scope cache keys by policy/mode + exact receiver/room lineage as needed + full source FactRef/incarnation/hash/pin. A single cached or retained upgraded under label must not leak to a legacy reader; retain raw checked facts and derive labels at use.\n\nBootstrap matters: before a new issue/concern has a genesis, there is no local recorded receiver lineage. Select no privilege from the delivered.to seed or proposed directory field alone. Obtain the closed raw creation proof first, verify the actual native partition or parent create entry, seed/message/address and exact new root lineage, and only then apply the eligible creation/identity policy. Otherwise the design either deadlocks new native creation or admits a forged lineage.\n\nYour eight-fact set is a reasonable bounded BASE proof for a directly partition-created application/change/issue: (1) lane genesis, (2) partition creating entry, (3) partition genesis, (4) root opening entry, (5) root genesis, (6–8) exact membership6/rules3/destination6 sibling geneses. Current directory genesis really emits the three sibling creates, so the three accepted sibling geneses can be matched to those exact root0 sends. Check applied genesis, exact definition pins, kind/address/seed/creator/cause/ordinal, source FactRef and request n, sentBy and full message/context, and same full references/incarnations throughout. Check the root opening actually copies the confirmed root sibling refs under the trusted native root10 rule, and that destination6 belongs to the same root. Do not treat raw hashes, an under string, or a merely directory-kind frame as proof of native execution. An eight-entry-size payload cap also needs pre-parse byte/frame/count guards, deduplication of repeated refs, a total deadline and no fallback to a truncated proof.\n\nThe root need not recursively fetch register ancestry merely to recognize this direct native factory IF the normal trusted one-namespace Source boundary has already authenticated the root object's actual root10 pin/applied genesis and its root opening. Register11-\u003eroot10 remains explicit and the ordinary root creation admission still checks its source. This is the same trusted-native-runtime boundary, not an assertion that eight arbitrary raw entries prove valid execution. Replay must still perform its normal checked causal/native genesis validation; do not add root10 as an unverified anchor to bypass register/creation obligations. The eight frames bound this origin projection, not every dependency needed for a complete standalone replay/export.\n\nImportant limit: eight is NOT a sufficient flattened proof of arbitrary issue concerns. A concern's creator is an issue and its cause is add-concern, not the partition's open-issue. Each such child must prove the exact parent native identity/lineage, its exact creating add-concern entry, seed/message/cause/ordinal, inherited directory/membership/root affiliation and self-origin binding. That parent may itself be a concern. Keep the current child-issue provenance checks and extend their NEW-policy lineage transitively; never promote a child merely because its declared name, directory field or parent under says issue. Either reuse a checked, policy-bound parent identity/anchor with an explicit bounded recursive validation contract, or supply the additional ancestor facts under an explicit total work/depth/byte budget. Memoization must include the identity policy and exact immutable frames; cycles/contradictions fail, missing/exhausted required proof is unresolved. Do not describe eight facts per recursive hop as eight total, or silently make unbounded nested Source calls. If the first Source cannot meet that bounded concern-chain contract, surface that concrete remaining implementation boundary rather than claiming direct-lane proof covers concerns.\n\nFor closure: old issue receivers must continue to reject/not recognize partition-born changes exactly under their original policy, including pin-confirm/unpin/closes and all fact-under constraints, not just destination publication. A new issue receiver may recognize a proved new change only under its own checked eligible lineage and the unchanged handler/fact/relation/authority rules; recognizing a role is not a new close grant. Preserve any existing legitimate cross-scope fact behavior; do not replace actual relation/provenance checks with same-kind or same-room alone. New concern receivers use the parent lineage rule above. Test both old/new receiving directions, a declared-name imitation, wrong parent/root/sibling/incarnation/create message, missing parent evidence and bounded-depth exhaustion.\n\nReplay must choose the same receiver policy for each checked run/admission, including an initially empty new scope's verified creation lineage. The current global sourceName/application callback slots and sourceIdentity cache cannot determine policy from supplied-function order or a sender's newest classification. Mixed old/new histories must preserve their different accepted under meanings for the same source facts where policy differs. Share a small pure proof validator between runtime/replay; keep collection and authority interpretation separate.\n\nThis refines d1543f97 rather than authorizing a global identity change. Complete Q6/Q7 real Authority and consumer search witnesses are still owed, as are ordinary/file publication/D1 closure/old-pin controls and the eventual exact Source review. No code edits, tests, package install, raw/private fixture reads, push, provider or deployment action by checker.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","no_git_artifact":"true","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:40cfa951101646c02f246aea8559ecb6f28d7e5e","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:913333259b672270742c52ea4e49158bd420c604"}}